                                                                                            <rect key="frame" x="0.0" y="215" width="345" height="128"/>
                                                                                            <string key="text">The way the heart beats in atrial fibrillation means there's a risk of blood clots forming in the heart chambers. If these enter the bloodstream, they can cause a stroke. Your doctor will assess and discuss your risk with you, and try to minimise your chance of having a stroke.</string>
